    {
      "id": "key-text",
      "shape": "text",
      "role": "label",
      "face": "body",
      "text": "Time goes from left to right. The distances are not to scale.\nBlue: the runner. Grey: the managed process and the rest of its process group.\nPale: that part has ended. An X marks the reap of the process.\nEach signal goes to the process and to the rest of its group.\nA wait ends when the process exits. Then the runner sends no signal to the process.\nThe runner looks twice each second. A step can start up to 0.5 second late.\nThe runner stops the rest of the process group before it reaps the process.",
      "x": 481.15625,
      "y": 805.141015625,
      "anchor": "center",
      "align": "center",
      "wrapped": false,
      "w": 591.486328125,
